WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.228 --> 00:00:02.664
(whimsical music)

00:00:02.664 --> 00:00:04.646
(man groaning)

00:00:04.646 --> 00:00:05.604
- [Narrator] Golf isn't known for being

00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:08.065
the most forgiving game.

00:00:08.065 --> 00:00:09.148
- [Man] Shit!

00:00:10.373 --> 00:00:11.621
- [Narrator] But there's nothing quite

00:00:11.621 --> 00:00:14.504
like shanking your ball
into the drink or pond.

00:00:14.504 --> 00:00:17.087
That's where this guy comes in.

00:00:23.076 --> 00:00:26.053
Here at TPC Sawgrass, hundreds
of golfers lose their balls

00:00:26.053 --> 00:00:29.757
to the infamous par three 17th hole.

00:00:29.757 --> 00:00:32.261
But one golfer's misery
is another man's gold.

00:00:32.261 --> 00:00:34.222
This is Gordon Davis.

00:00:34.222 --> 00:00:35.660
- My name is Gordon Davis,

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.729
and I'm a professional golf ball diver.

00:00:38.729 --> 00:00:40.147
- [Narrator] And he makes a
living diving for golf balls

00:00:40.147 --> 00:00:41.564
all over Florida.

00:00:43.315 --> 00:00:44.504
- [Gordon] I've been diving for golf balls

00:00:44.504 --> 00:00:46.269
approximately 50 years.

00:00:46.269 --> 00:00:48.743
- [Narrator] There are a
lot of balls to be found.

00:00:48.743 --> 00:00:52.740
- On average, when I'm diving,
I'll pick up 3 to 4,000.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:53.945
- [Narrator] 3,000 to 4, 000?

00:00:53.945 --> 00:00:55.365
- 3,000 to 4,000.

00:00:55.365 --> 00:00:56.468
- [Narrator] Whoa.

00:00:56.468 --> 00:00:59.468
So, how do you find these golf balls?

00:01:00.394 --> 00:01:02.590
- [Gordon] It's mostly,
you know, just feel,

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.569
picking them up out of the mud

00:01:04.569 --> 00:01:05.971
and some places the mud's so deep

00:01:05.971 --> 00:01:08.851
that you can't do nothing with it, you know?

00:01:08.851 --> 00:01:10.185
- [Narrator] And it's that
mud that makes it impossible

00:01:10.185 --> 00:01:12.102
to see, well, anything.

00:01:14.281 --> 00:01:15.114
- [Gordon] Most courses,

00:01:15.114 --> 00:01:17.877
there’s very few that has clear water.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:20.382
Most of them has poor visibility

00:01:20.382 --> 00:01:23.552
because of the algae and all that.

00:01:23.552 --> 00:01:26.854
- [Narrator] So what happens next?

00:01:26.854 --> 00:01:29.643
- After I pull the balls
out, they go through,

00:01:29.643 --> 00:01:34.047
pick out some of them, and
they take them from there.

00:01:34.047 --> 00:01:34.940
- [Narrator] They being someone who wants

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:36.991
to repurpose these balls.

00:01:36.991 --> 00:01:39.467
- These balls are authentic.

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:41.566
- [Narrator] These authentic
balls are diced up,

00:01:41.566 --> 00:01:43.231
placed in all sorts of usable keepsakes

00:01:43.231 --> 00:01:46.898
like saw grass, watches,
and bottle openers.

00:01:48.166 --> 00:01:50.175
And Gordon, he knows what it takes

00:01:50.175 --> 00:01:52.731
to be a professional golf ball diver.

00:01:52.731 --> 00:01:56.775
- What I tell people is you
gotta be kind of a special cat

00:01:56.775 --> 00:02:00.390
to be a golf all diver, somebody with grit

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:03.772
and that wants to be
an independent person.

00:02:03.772 --> 00:02:06.727
It's like any other business,
someone has to do it.

00:02:06.727 --> 00:02:10.124
Everybody has a different job
and this happens to be mine.

00:02:10.124 --> 00:02:11.722
- [Narrator] Seeing as
you're kind of a special cat,

00:02:11.722 --> 00:02:14.284
any advice for golfers trying
to keep their balls dry?

00:02:14.284 --> 00:02:17.534
- [Gordon] Yeah, take up another sport.

00:02:19.923 --> 00:02:23.090
(laughs) Hole-in-one!

